(Simplified Water Bill Computation)
The bill for a water service subscriber is prepared as follows:
1. Read the name of the water consumer
2. Read the previous water meter reading in cubic meters (reading last month) from the
consumer’s meter. The meter reading cannot be less than zero.
3. Read the present water meter reading in cubic meters (reading this month) from the
consumer’s meter. The present water meter reading cannot be less than the previous water
meter reading.
4. Compute the volume of water consumed (consumption = CMUSed) by subtracting the
previous reading from the present reading.
5. Read the classification of the consumer (c for commercial or r for residential)
6. Compute the amount due from the consumer. The amount due is computed based on the
following:

For residential consumers
If Cubic Meters Consumed is                 then Amount Due (pesos)
========================================================================
Less than or equal to 12                    180.00
More than 12                                180.00 + (cubicMetersConsumed – 12) * 30.00

For commercial consumers
If Cubic Meters Consumed is                 then Amount Due (pesos)
========================================================================
Less than or equal to 30                    600.00
More than 30                                600.00 + (cubicMetersConsumed – 30) * 50.00

7. Print a bill statement. The bill statement should show the name of the subscriber, the
readings, the consumption and the amount due.
-----------------------------------------------------------------
INPUT:      Water Consumer
            Previous water meter reading
            Present water meter reading
            Consumer classification
PROCESS:    Compute the volume of water consumed
            Compute amount of due
OUTPUT:     Bill Statement
-----------------------------------------------------------------
ALGORITHM:
1. Read and accept the name of the consumer
2. Read and evaluate the previous water meter reading in cubic meters.
Meter reading cannot be less than zero.
3. Read and evaluate the present water meter reading in cubic meters.
Present meter reading cannot be less than the previous water meter reading.
4. Compute the volume of water consumed.
5. Read and accept the consumer classification.
6. Compute amount due.
7. Print bill statement.
*/


import java.util.Scanner;

public class WaterBill {

    public static Scanner input = new Scanner(System.in);

    public static String consumerName;                                // to hold name of consumer
    public static char consumerType = 'a';                            // to hold type of consumer
    public static int presentReading = -1, previousReading = -1;      // to hold the present and previous reading
    public static int waterConsumed;                                  // to hold number of cubic meters of water used

    public static int residentialMinimumVolume = 12;                  // to hold cut-off for minimum Bill for residential consumer
    public static double residentialMinimumBill = 180.00;             // minimum bill 12 Cubic Meters used
    public static float residentialRate = 30.00F;                     // cost of 1 Cubic Meter above the min. consumption

    public static int commercialMinimumVolume = 30;                   // to hold cut-off for minimum Bill for commercial consumers
    public static double commercialMinimumBill = 600.00;              // minimum bill  20 Cubic Meters used
    public static float commercialRate = 50.00F;                      // cost of 1 Cubic Meter above the min. consumption for commercial consumers

    public static double amountDue;                                   // to hold the amount due


    public static void main(String[] args) {

        //Read and accept the consumer name
        System.out.print("Enter the consumer's name: ");
        consumerName = input.nextLine();


        //Read and evaluate the previous water reading of the consumer
        while (previousReading < 0) {
            System.out.print("Enter the previous water reading of the consumer: ");

            if (input.hasNextInt()) {
                previousReading = Integer.parseInt(input.nextLine());

                if (previousReading < 0) {
                    System.out.println("--- Invalid Value. Previous water reading cannot be less than zero. ---");
                }

            } else {
                System.out.println("--- Invalid Value. Previous water reading must be a numerical value. ---");
                input.nextLine();
            }
        }


        //Read and evaluate the present water reading of the consumer
        while (presentReading < 0 || presentReading < previousReading) {
            System.out.print("Enter the present water reading of the consumer: ");

            if (input.hasNextInt()) {
                presentReading = Integer.parseInt(input.nextLine());

                if (presentReading < 0) {
                    System.out.println("--- Invalid Value. Present water reading cannot be less than zero. ---");
                } else if (presentReading < previousReading){
                    System.out.println("--- Invalid Value. Present water reading cannot be less than the previous water reading. ---");
                }

            } else {
                System.out.println("--- Invalid Value. Present water reading must be a numerical value. ---");
                input.nextLine();
            }
        }

        // Compute for the volume of water consumed
        waterConsumed = presentReading - previousReading;

        // Check and validate consumer classification
        while (consumerType != 'r' && consumerType != 'R' && consumerType != 'c' && consumerType != 'C') {
            System.out.print("Enter the consumer type - [R]esidential or [C]ommercial: ");
            consumerType = input.next().toLowerCase().charAt(0);

            if (consumerType == 'r' || consumerType == 'R') {
                System.out.println("Selected: Residential");
                amountDue = residentialComputation(waterConsumed);

            } else if (consumerType == 'c' || consumerType == 'C') {
                System.out.println("Selected: Commercial");
                amountDue = commercialComputation(waterConsumed);

            } else {
                System.out.println("Invalid consumer classification.");
            }
        }

        // Display final billing summary
        System.out.println("\n==================================");
        System.out.println("        WATER BILL RECEIPT        ");
        System.out.println("==================================");
        System.out.println("Consumer Name: " + consumerName);
        System.out.println("Consumer Type: " + (consumerType == 'r' ? "Residential" : "Commercial"));
        System.out.println("Consumption  : " + waterConsumed + " cu.m.");
        System.out.printf("Total Amount Due: PHP %.2f%n", amountDue);
        System.out.println("==================================");


    } // end of main


    public static double residentialComputation(double waterConsumed) {
        if (waterConsumed <= residentialMinimumVolume) {
            return residentialMinimumBill;
        } else {
            return residentialMinimumBill + (waterConsumed - residentialMinimumVolume) * 30.00;
        }
    }

    public static double commercialComputation(double waterConsumed) {
        if (waterConsumed <= commercialMinimumVolume) {
            return commercialMinimumBill;
        } else {
            return commercialMinimumBill + (waterConsumed - commercialMinimumVolume) * 50.00;
        }
    }
} // end of class
